From c443bb5939f52e28f0ca93b6b2dd0777bc0d7464 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 06:18:25 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 1.2/1.3/2: base classes, AcceptButton/CancelButton,
 compat enums

Implements the first tranche of GAP-CLOSURE-PLAN.md against the net48 baseline.

Phase 1.2 - structural base classes (restores members lost to a flattened hierarchy):
- TextBoxBase : Control; re-parents TextBox, RichTextBox, MaskedTextBox onto it.
  Restores Clear/Copy/Cut/Paste/Undo/ClearUndo/AppendText/TextLength/Modified/
  CanUndo and the ModifiedChanged/ReadOnlyChanged/... events to the text family;
  consolidates the duplicated selection surface. Undo covers content-edit ops.
- ButtonBase : Control, IButtonControl; re-parents Button, CheckBox, RadioButton.
  Consolidates the 3x-duplicated TextAlign->GTK-alignment logic into one wired
  template; adds FlatStyle/FlatAppearance/AutoEllipsis/UseMnemonic/
  UseCompatibleTextRendering/TextImageRelation (appearance surface stored for
  source compatibility, deferring rendering to the GTK theme).
- New type FlatButtonAppearance.
- GTK-wrapper name clash (GtkSystem...ButtonBase/TextBoxBase) resolved with a
  using-alias in the two affected files, as the plan predicted.

Phase 1.3 - Form.AcceptButton / CancelButton (designer-emitted for most dialogs):
- AcceptButton wires the GTK window default widget so ENTER activates it natively;
  a form-level Enter/Escape handler also applies the button's DialogResult and
  closes, keyboard-only so it does not double-fire with the mouse release path.

Phase 2 - 13 compatibility enums with values read from the real net48 reference
assembly (several non-sequential: ArrowDirection, SearchDirectionHint, ScrollButton):
CharacterCasing, ScrollBars, TabAppearance, FrameStyle, LinkBehavior, InsertKeyMode,
ItemBoundsPortion, ColumnHeaderAutoResizeStyle, ScrollButton, ArrowDirection,
SearchDirectionHint, MenuMerge, DockingBehavior.

Net48 public types present 522->538 (missing 512->496). Full suite green at 2261
(+19 new functional tests). Clipboard round-trip is intentionally not asserted:
taking/reading the GTK clipboard destabilizes the shared single-threaded test host.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
